# Accepted image-scan findings.
#
# Policy: CI reports every CRITICAL/HIGH into the Security tab, and separately fails the
# build on any CRITICAL or HIGH that has a fix available upstream. A finding is listed here
# only when it is fixable and deliberately accepted anyway — each entry needs a reason and a
# review date, and `tools/check_vulnerability_exceptions.py` fails the build once that date
# passes, so an exception is renewed deliberately rather than by default.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # <reason> (accepted YYYY-MM-DD, review by YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# Findings that are unfixable upstream do NOT belong here: ignore-unfixed already excludes
# them from the gate, and listing them would hide them once a fix does appear.
#
# No accepted exceptions at present.
